When a drawing is wider or taller than 32768 pt, xlabel and unplaced edge-label placement (`placeLabels`) can pick a different candidate position than C. The label moves by about its own width. C keeps the objects in a dictionary whose comparison reads the 32-bit Hilbert key as a signed `int`. The port sorts the keys as `u32`. Keys with the top bit set, which only occur when coordinates reach 2^15, therefore sort first in the port and last in C. The R-tree is built in that order. C's R-tree covers are not real bounding boxes (see below), so a different insertion order changes which neighbours `RTreeSearch` finds.

