**Root cause**

C, `lib/label/xlabels.c:28-35`: `Hdisc` has `.size = sizeof(int)` and `icompare` compares `*(int *)` keys, although `hd_hil_s_from_xy` (`xlabels.c:114`) returns `unsigned`. With `order = 16` (coordinates up to 65535) the keys of objects at large x come out negative.

The port, `crates/graphviz-pure-layout/src/common/xlabels.rs:716`: `keyed.sort_by(|a, b| a.0.cmp(&b.0).then(...))` on `u32`.

On seed 30157 the port's R-tree root split 64/1 and C's split 31/34. Traced with an instrumented C build: C's `RTreeSearch` misses an overlapping node, so its first candidate is free (`n=0`). The port finds the node (`n=1, area=120`) and moves to the next candidate. The covers are also wrong because `CombineRect` takes `fmin` of the upper bounds (`lib/label/rectangle.c:95`). That is an upstream bug, which the port reproduces on purpose (`xlabels.rs:52-65`). The key comparison is the only thing that differs here.

Suggested fix: sort by `(key as i32)`.

Checked with a patched build of HEAD whose only change is comparing the key as `i32` at `xlabels.rs:716`. All 16 cases below then match C byte for byte. They are fdp, circo (`repro-circo.gv`: a `headlabel` placed as an xlabel moves 70pt to the other side of the edge end) and 12 neato cases. Those 12 were first grouped with the equal-key-order issue (xlabels-dtobag-equal-key-order); the sign fix alone fixes them. The neato-family corpus (2015 files) is unchanged. The code is shared by every engine that calls `addXLabels`.

**Cases**

16 fuzz cases, seeds 730, 878, 1843, 10593, 20397, 21395, 22436, 22620, 22829, 30157, 30222, 31707, 32286, 32812, 32867, 35912 (fdp 20397, 30157, 32867; circo 878; the rest neato). The reproducers are large, about 55 lines each, because the drawing must be at least 32768pt wide. Regenerate a case with `python3 -I scripts/fuzz-gen.py --seed N` (byte for byte for these seeds).

