`tests/fuzz-open/027-dot-sameport-record-uninit-pathend`

Visual diff: {{SITE}}/whats-left/dot-sameport-record-uninit-pathend/

When nodes overlap, clipping can leave an edge with a one-point Bézier (here the multi-edge `n1 -- n9`, routed by the straight-line fallback because nodes touch: `pos="549,163.11"`). The packer (`pack=`, or sfdp/neato/fdp packing disconnected components with `doSplines`) rasterises each edge into polyomino cells with `fillEdge`, which reads `bz.list[1]` without checking the size. In C that reads past the end of the list, and whatever is there becomes a cell — here extra cells near the origin of component 0 (`-v3` shows 114 cells with `splines=polyline` and 106 with `splines=spline`, same layout). The extra cells move the singleton component `n14` from (247,106) to (379,414). The port uses the point itself.

